{"segs": ["PA_ja_207:0.2", "PA_ja_207:0.3"], "en": "Second Fifty, Chapter on Nataṇḍala.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_207:0.4"], "en": "7. The Assaka Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_207:1.1", "PA_ja_207:1.2"], "en": "“This region was traversed by me while I was King Assaka.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_207:1.3", "PA_ja_207:1.4"], "en": "Together with her beloved husband, who desired her in return,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_207:2.1"], "en": "she experienced new joys and sorrows.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_207:2.2"], "en": "The old is being covered over;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_207:2.3", "PA_ja_207:2.4"], "en": "therefore, even a mere insect is dearer to me than the kingdom of the Assakas.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
